 assessment as a service, and specialized services for the department of defense and intelligence community; and autonomous systems solutions, AI/machine learning (ML) decision intelligence solutions, and AI orchestration as a service, as well as specialized consulting services. In addition, it offers digital identity services comprising security solutions specializing in customized digital identity, biometrics, AI/ML, and advanced analytics software and solutions for global trade, travel, and digital identity industries; and Ask Sage Platform, a generative AI platform for secure AI deployment, orchestration, and agentic capabilities across defense, intelligence, and other highly regulated environments. The company was founded in 1988 and is headquartered in McLean, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Kevin  McAleenan | CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $516,677 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 579 people. Revenue per employee of $221K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers. Stock-based compensation of $40K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["BigBear.ai, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $919M market cap on $128M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -6% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -56% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 26%.","The company is burning through $42M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -11.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Stock-based comp at 18% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (29.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 174% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 71/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 161% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Did BigBear.ai (NYSE:BBAI) Hit A New Yearly Low Despite Revenue Growth?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link